**Finding: compliant (preferred level) — no redline proposed.**

Section 22 is the document's only audit right against us; Section 23 ("Records and Customer Assurance") contains no operative text, and searches for inspection, verification, monitoring, telemetry and remote-access language turned up nothing further.

Section 22 satisfies every preferred element:
- once in any twelve-month period; thirty days' prior written notice; normal business hours;
- off-site where practicable, by an independent auditor bound by confidentiality;
- Vendor bears costs unless underpayment exceeds five percent;
- no direct Vendor or auditor access to Customer systems.

Additional protections (no access to unrelated Customer Data, privileged material or third-party confidential information; findings are our Confidential Information; shortfall payment resolves the issue) run in our favour and are not flagged.
